    "Description": "X.Org X11 libXi runtime library\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* libXi: libXi: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds read during XI2 class parsing (CVE-2026-93542)\n\n* libXi: libXi: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds read in XI2 class parser (CVE-2026-93543)\n\n* libXi: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XQueryDeviceState() (CVE-2026-93541)\n\n* libXi: libXi: Arbitrary code execution via oversized DEVICE_ENABLE reply (CVE-2026-109090)\n\n* libXi: libXi: Arbitrary code execution via DEVICE_RESOLUTION heap-based buffer overflow (CVE-2026-109089)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
